# Gameplay. Y is the fire button, not B — the earlier movies hold B for
# thousands of frames and never once shoot, which is why `level1-rescue.zmv`
# reaches the enemy's acting branch exactly once in 1,226 collisions. Both
# players hold Y from the second cue on: a kill scores, and a kill by *each*
# of them is the point, because the score-slot search at $80:C7C2 is the
# identity in one-player mode and so cannot be told from a hard-coded index.
#
# The two direction tracks are deliberately counter-phase — Zeke runs right
# while Julie runs left and back again — so the pair repeatedly cross. Two
# players touching is the only thing that hands a player's handler an id of
# its own side ($5C or above), which is `player_ignore`.
